/-!
# VIII08 — same-source uniqueness of the odd magnetic potential, and the constant-source check

Two `MagClass 3` magnetic potentials with the same `Lmag` on `(3, ∞)` agree there.  This is
`VIII04.mag_unique` applied to the difference (with source `2·(3/2)·0/R³ = 0`), so it is not a
new uniqueness principle: the endpoint class does all the work.

As a check, the constant source `s ≡ 1` (i.e. `j = 0`, `q ≡ 1`) has the closed solution
`b(R) = -1/(8R)`, and `b_s` for that source is proved equal to it.
-/

